## Why This Is Asked
Tests how a junior candidate reasoned about KCA in an air-gapped lab, focusing on attestation, CSR enrollment, and offline policy mechanics. It probes practical flows without cloud dependencies.

## Key Concepts
- Attestation vs enrollment
- Short-lived certificates (TTL 600s)
- Offline revocation (local CRL)
- Policy updates via removable media

## Code Example
```javascript
// Enrollment sketch (pseudo-code)
async function enrollCSR(identity){
  const att = await attest(identity);
  if(!att.ok) throw new Error('attestation failed');
  const csr = createCSR(identity);
  return await kca.enroll(csr, att);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate offline revocation consistency across devices?
- What tests would you run to ensure USB-delivered policy updates don’t drift over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical KCA integration with hardware attestation, regional bootstrap, crypto agility, and lifecycle controls in a distributed, high-churn edge.

## Key Concepts
- TPM-backed root and regional bootstrap attestation
- PQC certificate issuance with crypto agility path
- Per-tenant SPIFFE IDs and cross-region trust anchors
- Offline root fallback and revocation via OCSP/CRLs
- Auditing, policy binding, and renewal strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: CSR flow to central KCA
function enrollCSR(device) {
  attestDeviceRoot(device);
  const csr = device.createCSR();
  const cert = centralKCA.issuePQC(certParamsFrom(device), csr);
  device.installCert(cert);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you upgrade PQC algorithms in-flight without revoking all certs?
- How do you test revocation latency at scale and ensure audit integrity?

## Why This Is Asked

Explores KCA in latency- and connectivity-constrained edge deployments, with offline attestations and cross-region trust.

## Key Concepts

- Edge KCA workflows, offline attestation, short-lived certs
- Per-tenant store binding (SPIFFE IDs, scopes)
- Crypto agility (PQC fallback) and OTA signing
- Cross-region trust anchors and revocation/audit
- Testing for outages, handoffs, and tamper-evident logs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: device attestation flow
function attestationFlow() {
  const boot = verifyHardwareRoot();
  const regional = attestToRegionalBootstrap();
  const csr = createCSR(storeId, scope);
  const cert = enrollToKCA(csr, ttl=300);
  if (!regional.connected) { useRecoveryToken(); }
  rotateIfNeeded();
  return cert;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you securely rotate keys during long outages?
- How do you verify audit logs across regions for a rollback scenario?
